Because Docker can reuse unchanged layers.

Imagine:

Build 1
 ↓
Base
 ↓
Dependencies
 ↓
Application

You change only:

src/server.ts

Docker doesn't necessarily need to rebuild everything from scratch if earlier 
layers remain reusable.
This is called:
Layer caching

Later we'll have a dedicated topic for this because it's extremely important for optimizing Node.js Docker builds.